      "reading": "applying the measured lift moves accuracy 0.422 -> 0.760 and the false-positive rate 0.887 -> 0.153, and recall 1.000 -> 0.597: the correction buys the ability to say DRY at the price of missing some genuinely flooded segments"
    },
    "reading": "the correction is not applied, and this is what that decision buys: applying it would silence the alert entirely for 969 of the 1469 streets that the shipped rule warns in time, and delay the rest by a median of 71 h. What it would buy back is measured on the peak in harvey_validation.json's correction_would_score: accuracy 0.422 -> 0.760 and the false-positive rate 0.887 -> 0.153, at the cost of 167 segments that flooded and would now be called dry. Trading a false alarm for a miss is not free in a life-safety product, and one event cannot say which trade is right."
  },
