  "reference_algorithm": "tier_onset(tier) = hours of the first hourly point with stage >= tier; hours_before_crest = crest_h - tier_onset; flags(stage) = count of segments with flood_stage_ft <= stage; corrected flags(stage) = count with flood_stage_ft + lift <= stage; street_lead(segment) = crest_h minus the hours of the first hourly point at or above that segment's own flood_stage_ft, null when it is never reached. The app recomputes all of these from its own replay series and its own road list, and must match verification_grid exactly.",
  "limits": [
    "no per-street timing is validated: the only street-level observation is one event-maximum extent, so the tier onsets are observed but the street onset that precedes the crest is the model",
    "the lead time is measured to the gauge crest, and the crest travels downstream during the event, so a street away from the gauge has a different (later) crest",
    "the replay window ends 2 h after the crest, so the falling limb is not observed: the artifact reports when tiers were crossed, not when they cleared",
    "the flag counts inherit the threshold defect this module measures rather than fixes; the corrected counts apply one event's fitted constant, which is exactly why the app does not apply it",
    "one event: this is a backcast of Harvey, and cannot be repeated on another flood from data in this repo"
  ]
